     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, though I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy first. If you give me the corrected dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
