       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. You've confirmed it, but the reason you gave is about timing, not a clinical need for 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any indication that justifies it, and the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is real.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **A lower starting dose to titrate up.** For example, 500 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf you think the patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk to pharmacy or an attending/endocrinology first. If the order is then still needed, they can place or approve it directly.\n\nI can also add a note to any order I enter, such as \"titrate per glucose response,\" if that helps get things settled before evening rounds. Which dose would you like?"
      }
